\section org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisOverview Overview
The brain analysis plugin allows advanced visualization and interaction
with diffusion MRI (dMRI) datasets.

\section org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisUsage Usage
This section provides a description of the plugin usage. The interface is
divided into four sections

<ol>
  <li>Tools</li>
  <li>Data</li>
  <li>Selection objects</li>
  <li>Display</li>
</ol>

\image html BrainAnalysisInterface.png "Brain Analysis plugin interface"

\section org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisTools Tools
Help tooltip can be displayed by moving the mouse cursor over any of the
tool icon.

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysis2dview Fiber display in 2D views
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html 2d_resize.png "2D fiber display icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>
Display fibers passing through each 2D views.

\warning 2D fiber display is not enabled by default because it can impact the
performance greatly.

\image html fibersOn2dViews.png "Display fibers on 2D views"

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisSO Selection/Exclusion objects
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html 3d78_resize.png "Selection cuboid icon"
    </td>
    <td>
      \image html 3d78_not_resize.png "Exclusion cuboid icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html sphere_resize.png "Selection ellipsoid icon"
    </td>
    <td>
      \image html sphere_not_resize.png "Exclusion ellipsoid icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Objects can be used to select/exclude fibers passing through them. MI-Brain
currently support cuboid and ellipsoid shape. Size, location and rotation can
be set using

<ul>
  <li>
    <b>Ctrl-Left mouse button: </b>
      Translate the bounding box
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Ctrl-Right mouse button: </b>
      Resize the bounding box
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Ctrl-Middle mouse button: </b>
      Rotate the bounding box
  </li>
</ul>

\note OSX users will need to use the Command button instead of Ctrl.

\image html fiberSelection.png "Basic fiber selection"

\note You can only use <b>one</b> selection object while in HARDI RTT mode

User can easily build an object hierarchy to refine filtering. Simply select
the selection object you want to refine the selection from in the data manager
and create a new selection object.

\image html selectionObjectHierarchy.png "Selection object hierarchy"
\image html fiberSelectionHierarchy.png "Fiber selection hierarchy using two selection objects"

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisFiberColoring Fiber coloring
\subsubsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisUniformColoring Uniform coloring
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html paint37_resize.png "Uniform coloring icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Apply an uniform color to the fibers. Applies to all fiber datasets if no
selection has been made in the data manager.

\image html uniformColoring.png "Uniform red coloring"

\subsubsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisLocalSegmentColoring Local segment coloring
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html local_resize.png "Color based on local fiber segment icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Apply a color to each fiber segment based on the local segment orientation.
Applies to all fiber datasets if no selection has been made in the data
manager.

\image html localSegmentColoring.png "Color based on local fiber segment"

\subsubsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisEndpointsColoring Endpoints coloring
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html endpoints_resize.png "Color based on fiber endpoints icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Apply a color to each fiber based on the average fiber orientation. Applies to
all fiber datasets if no selection has been made in the data
manager.

\image html endpointsColoring.png "Color based on fiber endpoints"

\subsubsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisShuffleColoring Shuffle coloring
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html couple35_resize.png "Shuffle fiber color icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Apply a (different) uniform color to each fiber datasets. Applies to all fiber
datasets if no selection has been made in the data manager.

\image html shuffleColoring.png "Shuffle coloring"

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisFiberGeometry Fiber geometry
<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html fitGeometry_resize.png "Align fibers on reference anatomy icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

\note Always load your reference anatomy prior to your fiber datasets

A good rule of thumb is to <b>always</b> load your reference anatomy prior to
loading your fiber dataset. MI-Brain will automatically transform your fiber
dataset to fit on your reference anatomy using the anatomy affine
transformation matrix. If you happen to load your fiber dataset before the
reference anatomy, there is a good chance the two won't be aligned. Use this
tool to correct alignment.

\image html unalignedBundles.png "Unaligned fiber bundles"

\warning Do not use the fiber alignment tool on data that are already aligned.
It <b>will</b> unalign them.

<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html one64_resize.png "Mirror axially"
    </td>
    <td>
      \image html one64_h_resize.png "Mirror sagitally"
    </td>
    <td>
      \image html double125_resize.png "Mirror coronally"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Mirror fibers relative to the reference anatomy center.

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisVisibleFiberBundle Save visible fibers

<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html human90_resize.png "Save visible fibers to datamanager"
    </td>
    <td>
      \image html watch3_resize.png "Save visible fibers to disk"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>


Make a new fiber bundle with fibers that are currently visible on-screen and
save it in the datamanager or on disk.

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisGenerateBinaryImage Generate binary mask

<center>
<table>
  <tr>
    <td>
      \image html brain8_resize.png "Generate binary mask with visible fibers icon"
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
</center>

Generate a binary mask with on-screen fibers. A voxel will be assigned to the
foreground of the mask if at least one fiber passes through it.

\image html binaryMask.png "Binary mask (in red) generated from visible fibers"

\section org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisTrackingDisplay Tracking and filtering parameters
This section describes the different filtering/tracking parameters that the
user can ajust to enhance the displayed fibers.

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisFiberfiltering Fiber filtering
User can filter fibers using selection/exclusion object. Min/max fiber lenght
can be set using the two sliders in the "Display" section. Information about
fibers (number, min/max lenght, etc) are displayed in the box below the
sliders.

\image html displaySection.png "Fiber display parameters"

\subsection org_imeka_qt_brainanalysisHARDIRTT HARDI Real-time tracking (RTT)
One can generate HARDI fibers in real-time using maximas and a tracking mask
such as the FA. The maximas dataset is a 4D image where the fourth
dimension has 9 components (x<sub>1</sub>, y<sub>1</sub>, z<sub>1</sub>, ...,
x<sub>3</sub>, y<sub>3</sub>, z<sub>3</sub>). User can ajust
the tracking parameters using the appropriate sliders.

<ul>
  <li>
    <b>Min. lenght: </b>
      Minimum fiber lenght
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Max. lenght: </b>
      Maximum fiber lenght
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Max. angle: </b>
      Maximum angle that a fiber segment is allowed to curve
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Min. mask: </b>
      Minimal value of the tracking mask to be considered as a voxel in which
      the tracking can proceed
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Step: </b>
      Size of a tractography step in the image
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Seed/axis: </b>
      Number of seeds per axis
  </li>
  <li>
    <b>Puncture: </b>
      Weighting factor between the previous direction and the direction found
      for the next tractography step. The next direction is chosen as the
      closest to the previous direction. A high puncture value gives more
      importance to the new direction,  which implies that the fibers will
      more easily deviate to follow new directions at each step. A lower
      puncture value implies that the streamline will more closely follow the
      input direction
  </li>
</ul>

\image html displayRTT.png "HARDI RTT parameters"

The user can seed the tracking from a selection object or from one or more
binary mask(s).

\note You can only use <b>one</b> selection object while in HARDI RTT mode

\image html rttSeedFromBinMask.png "HARDI RTT seed from binary mask"

*/
